rl":"git@github.com:webpack/webpack.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack","homepage":"https://webpack.js.org","size":75289,"stargazers_count":65817,"watchers_count":65817,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":9188,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":210,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["amd","build-tool","commonjs","compiler","es2015","es6","esm","javascript","javascript-compiler","javascript-modules","loaders","module-bundler","plugins","web","web-performance","webpack"],"visibility":"public","forks":9188,"open_issues":210,"watchers":65817,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"<!-- Please don't delete this template or we'll close your issue -->\r\n<!-- Before creating an issue please make sure you are using the latest version of webpack. -->\r\n<!-- Also consider trying the webpack@beta version, maybe it's already fixed. -->\r\n\r\n**Do you want to request a *feature* or report a *bug*?**\r\n\r\nBug\r\n\r\n_Note: I am still trying to create a small reproducable case but I am not able to do it. But i see this issue in my huge code base in my company._\r\n\r\n<!-- Please ask questions on StackOverflow or the webpack Gitter (https://gitter.im/webpack/webpack). -->\r\n<!-- Issues which contain questions or support requests will be closed. -->\r\n\r\n**What is the current behavior?**\r\n\r\n* We use a lot of `index.js` files and then we just `import` by specifying the import name till the folder.\r\n* I am using `ModuleConcatenationPlugin`\r\n* Many of my `index.js` files have code in this pattern\r\n\r\n```js\r\nimport * as svg from \"./svg\";\r\n\r\nexport {\r\n    svg\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\n* I have many `index.js` files scattered in different folder which have the same content pattern.\r\n* With webpack 2 everything works fine\r\n* With webpack 3, I have see a variable named `index_js_namespaceObject` for all the files which have `index.js`.\r\n\r\nhere is some output:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n// CONCATENATED MODULE: ./src/main/js/controls/atomic/icon/svg/index.js\r\nvar index_js_namespaceObject = {};\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"SvgIcon\", function() { return SvgIcon_js_defaultExport; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"alert\", function() { return index_js_alert; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"clinical\", function() { return clinical; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"communication\", function() { return communication; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"content\", function() { return index_js_content; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"image\", function() { return index_js_image; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"navigation\", function() { return navigation; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"notification\", function() { return index_js_notification; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"status\", function() { return status; });\r\n\r\n\r\n// CONCATENATED MODULE: ./src/main/js/controls/atomic/icon/index.js\r\nvar index_js_namespaceObject = {};\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"svg\", function() { return index_js_namespaceObject; });\r\n\r\n// somehere in code\r\nvar _svg$clinical = index_js_namespaceObject.clinical,\r\n    ClinicalBadge_js_Abnormal = _svg$clinical.Abnormal //-->>>>> ERROR here\r\n\r\n// CONCATENATED MODULE: ./src/main/js/controls/composite/panel/detail-panel/index.js\r\nvar index_js_namespaceObject = {};\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"DetailPanel\", function() { return DetailPanel_js_defaultExport; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"DetailPanelBanners\", function() { return DetailPanelBanners_js_defaultExport; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"DetailPanelTitle\", function() { return DetailPanelTitle_js_defaultExport; });\r\n__webpack_require__.d(index_js_namespaceObject, \"DetailPanelData\", function() { return DetailPanelData_js_defaultExport; });\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n**If the current behavior is a bug, please provide the steps to reproduce.**\r\n\r\nAs you can see above that the `index_js_namespaceObject` get redefined everytime and that why i get some errors as pointed out above.\r\n\r\n**Please mention other relevant information such as the browser version, Node.js version, webpack version and Operating System.**\r\n\r\nNode: 8\r\nnpm: 5\r\nWebpack: beta, 3.x\r\n\r\nI am trying to gather more info. Sorry for such a vague issue but i am trying. Thanks for patience\r\n\r\n\r\n### UPDATE\r\n\r\nReproducible case: https://github.com/gyandeeps/webpack-5020 \r\n\r\nI have tried to make it reproduce. I hope this makes sense.\r\n\r\n### UPDATE 2\r\n\r\n* After poking around, i think their is an issue with `import * as x` pattern in general. In my repocase above, even if you cutout icon1 branch and just keep one branch then also the final export doesnt connect all the way to the svg items.\r\n* You will get infinite chain from svg5 -> svg -> svg -> svg -> ......","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/5020/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/5020/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]